                            en: { titulus: "Syntactic Analysis", contentus: `<p>Two coordinated clauses. The first has the verb <b>duxerunt</b>, which governs an AcI: <b>biennium satis esse</b>. <b>Ad eas res conficiendas</b> is a gerundive construction with 'ad' to express purpose.</p><p>The second clause has the verb <b>confirmant</b>, with <b>profectionem</b> as its direct object.</p>` },
